<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Treemand</title><link>/</link><description>Recent content on Treemand</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Tree Output</title><link>/commands/tree/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/commands/tree/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="tree-output"&gt;Tree Output&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;treemand &amp;lt;cli&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; discovers any CLI&amp;rsquo;s full command hierarchy and renders it as a&#10;color-coded tree. Point it at anything: &lt;code&gt;git&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;kubectl&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;docker&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;aws&lt;/code&gt;, your&#10;own tools.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;img class="demo-img" src="/demos/cmd_tree.gif" alt="treemand tree demo" width="900" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="basic-usage"&gt;Basic usage &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#basic-usage" aria-label="Link to this section: Basic usage"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand git &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# full tree at default depth (3)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand --depth&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; kubectl &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# limit recursion depth&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand --filter&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;remote git &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# only show nodes matching pattern&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand --exclude&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;help&lt;/span&gt; git &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# hide nodes matching pattern&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand --commands-only kubectl &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# subcommands only — no flags or positionals&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="display-styles"&gt;Display styles &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#display-styles" aria-label="Link to this section: Display styles"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Four styles, switchable with &lt;code&gt;--tree-style&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;T&lt;/strong&gt; inside the TUI:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Output Formats: JSON and YAML</title><link>/commands/output/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/commands/output/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="output-formats-json-and-yaml"&gt;Output Formats: JSON and YAML&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;treemand can emit the discovered tree as JSON or YAML for scripting, diffing,&#10;and integration with other tools.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;img class="demo-img" src="/demos/cmd_output.gif" alt="treemand JSON/YAML output demo" width="900" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="usage"&gt;Usage &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#usage" aria-label="Link to this section: Usage"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand --output&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;json git &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# full tree as JSON&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand --output&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;yaml git &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# full tree as YAML&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand --output&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;text git &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# default colored text tree&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="json-schema"&gt;JSON schema &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#json-schema" aria-label="Link to this section: JSON schema"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The output follows a versioned JSON Schema, published at&#10;&lt;a href="https://treemand.dev/schema/tree.v1.json"&gt;treemand.dev/schema/tree.v1.json&lt;/a&gt; and printed by &lt;code&gt;treemand schema&lt;/code&gt;.&#10;The root carries &lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;schema_version&amp;quot;: 1&lt;/code&gt;; within a version the output only gains&#10;optional properties. See the &lt;a href="../../reference/#json--yaml-schema"&gt;reference&lt;/a&gt; for an&#10;example and the full compatibility promise.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Interactive TUI</title><link>/commands/interactive/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/commands/interactive/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="interactive-tui--i"&gt;Interactive TUI (&lt;code&gt;-i&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The interactive mode launches a full-screen terminal explorer with three panes:&#10;a live &lt;strong&gt;preview bar&lt;/strong&gt;, a navigable &lt;strong&gt;tree pane&lt;/strong&gt;, and a &lt;strong&gt;help pane&lt;/strong&gt; that shows&#10;&lt;code&gt;--help&lt;/code&gt; output for the currently selected node.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;img class="demo-img" src="/demos/cmd_interactive.gif" alt="treemand TUI demo" width="900" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="launch"&gt;Launch &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#launch" aria-label="Link to this section: Launch"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand -i git&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand -i kubectl&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand -i docker&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The TUI opens as soon as the CLI&amp;rsquo;s top-level help is read, usually in well under a second, even for CLIs with hundreds of subcommands. The rest is discovered in the background: the status bar shows &lt;code&gt;discovering… 37/233&lt;/code&gt;, and commands fill in without moving your selection. Everything discovered is cached, so the next run opens complete. If you quit early, the next run picks up where this one stopped.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>cache</title><link>/commands/cache/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/commands/cache/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="treemand-cache"&gt;&lt;code&gt;treemand cache&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;treemand caches discovered CLI trees in an SQLite database so repeat lookups are&#10;instant. The &lt;code&gt;cache&lt;/code&gt; subcommand lets you inspect and manage those entries.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;img class="demo-img" src="/demos/cmd_cache.gif" alt="treemand cache demo" width="900" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="commands"&gt;Commands &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#commands" aria-label="Link to this section: Commands"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand cache list &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# list all cached CLIs with age and size&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand cache clear git &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# clear the cached entry for git&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand cache clear &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# clear all cached entries&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="cache-details"&gt;Cache details &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#cache-details" aria-label="Link to this section: Cache details"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Property&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Location&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;~/.treemand/cache.db&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Format&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;SQLite&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Invalidation&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;the CLI&amp;rsquo;s executable changes (path, size or modification time)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;TTL&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;30 days (&lt;code&gt;cache_ttl_hours&lt;/code&gt; in the config; &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; = until the CLI changes)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;TUI expansions&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;commands discovered in &lt;code&gt;-i&lt;/code&gt; are saved back to the entry on exit&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Cache key&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;CLI binary fingerprint + discovery strategies + depth/stub settings&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="bypassing-the-cache"&gt;Bypassing the cache &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#bypassing-the-cache" aria-label="Link to this section: Bypassing the cache"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand --no-cache docker &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# skip cache for this run&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand --refresh docker &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# re-crawl now and update the entry&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;TREEMAND_CACHE_DIR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;/tmp treemand git &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# use a custom cache directory&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The cache key includes the CLI&amp;rsquo;s version string (from &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;cli&amp;gt; --version&lt;/code&gt;), so&#10;updating a CLI automatically invalidates its cached tree on the next run.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Reference</title><link>/reference/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/reference/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="reference"&gt;Reference&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="command-syntax"&gt;Command Syntax &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#command-syntax" aria-label="Link to this section: Command Syntax"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;treemand &amp;lt;cli&amp;gt; [flags]&#10;treemand version&#10;treemand schema&#10;treemand doctor &amp;lt;cli&amp;gt;&#10;treemand mcp&#10;treemand cache [clear|list]&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;h2 id="global-flags"&gt;Global Flags &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#global-flags" aria-label="Link to this section: Global Flags"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Flag&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Short&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Default&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--interactive&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;-i&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;false&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Launch interactive TUI explorer&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--strategy&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;-s&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;help&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Discovery strategies: &lt;code&gt;help&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;man&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;completions&lt;/code&gt; (comma-separated)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--depth&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;3&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Max tree depth (default 3; -1 = unlimited)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--filter&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Only show nodes whose name matches pattern&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--exclude&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Exclude nodes whose name matches pattern&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--commands-only&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;false&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Hide flags and positional arguments&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--full-path&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;false&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Show full command paths in tree&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--output&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;text&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Output format: &lt;code&gt;text&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;json&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;yaml&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--tree-style&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;default&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Tree presentation: &lt;code&gt;default&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;columns&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;compact&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;graph&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--icons&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;unicode&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Icon preset: &lt;code&gt;unicode&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ascii&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;nerd&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--line-length&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;80&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Max description chars before truncation&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--no-color&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;false&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Disable color output&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--no-cache&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;false&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Skip cache lookup and write&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--refresh&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;false&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Re-discover even if cached, and update the cache entry&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--stdin&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;false&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Read the CLI&amp;rsquo;s help text from stdin instead of running it; subcommands stay undiscovered (&lt;code&gt;docker --help | treemand --stdin docker&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--timeout&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;30&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Discovery timeout in seconds (0 = no limit)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;--debug&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;false&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Enable debug logging to stderr&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="subcommands"&gt;Subcommands &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#subcommands" aria-label="Link to this section: Subcommands"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="version"&gt;&lt;code&gt;version&lt;/code&gt; &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#version" aria-label="Link to this section: version"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Print version, git commit, and build date.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>config</title><link>/commands/config/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/commands/config/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="treemand-config"&gt;&lt;code&gt;treemand config&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Manage treemand&amp;rsquo;s optional YAML configuration file without opening it manually.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;img class="demo-img" src="/demos/cmd_config.gif" alt="treemand config demo" width="900" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="commands"&gt;Commands &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#commands" aria-label="Link to this section: Commands"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand config view &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# show merged config + file path&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand config validate &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# check for errors or unknown keys&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand config validate --strict &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# treat warnings as errors&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand config &lt;span class="nb"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt; &amp;lt;key&amp;gt; &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# write a value to the config file&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand config init &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# create a commented default config&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand config init --force &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# overwrite an existing config&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand config path &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# print the config file path&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand config edit &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# open config in $EDITOR&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="config-file-locations"&gt;Config file locations &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#config-file-locations" aria-label="Link to this section: Config file locations"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;treemand searches for the config file in this order:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>version</title><link>/commands/version/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/commands/version/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="treemand-version"&gt;&lt;code&gt;treemand version&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Print the version, git commit, and build date of the installed binary.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;img class="demo-img" src="/demos/cmd_version.gif" alt="treemand version demo" width="900" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="usage"&gt;Usage &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#usage" aria-label="Link to this section: Usage"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand version&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# treemand v0.3.0 (abc1234) built 2026-05-11&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The version is embedded at build time from the git tag (&lt;code&gt;git describe --tags&lt;/code&gt;).&#10;Development builds show &lt;code&gt;dev&lt;/code&gt; when no tag is present.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>completion</title><link>/commands/completion/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/commands/completion/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="treemand-completion"&gt;&lt;code&gt;treemand completion&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate shell completion scripts for bash, zsh, fish, or PowerShell. Once set&#10;up, pressing &lt;code&gt;Tab&lt;/code&gt; after &lt;code&gt;treemand&lt;/code&gt; suggests CLIs you&amp;rsquo;ve already explored from&#10;the cache.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;img class="demo-img" src="/demos/cmd_completion.gif" alt="treemand completion demo" width="900" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="setup"&gt;Setup &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#setup" aria-label="Link to this section: Setup"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="bash"&gt;Bash &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#bash" aria-label="Link to this section: Bash"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Add to ~/.bashrc&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt; &amp;lt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;treemand completion bash&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="zsh"&gt;Zsh &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#zsh" aria-label="Link to this section: Zsh"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Add to ~/.zshrc&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt; &amp;lt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;treemand completion zsh&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="fish"&gt;Fish &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#fish" aria-label="Link to this section: Fish"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand completion fish &amp;gt; ~/.config/fish/completions/treemand.fish&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="powershell"&gt;PowerShell &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#powershell" aria-label="Link to this section: PowerShell"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-powershell" data-lang="powershell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Add to your PowerShell profile&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;treemand&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;completion&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;powershell&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Out-String&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Invoke-Expression&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="how-it-works"&gt;How it works &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#how-it-works" aria-label="Link to this section: How it works"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The completion script hooks into your shell&amp;rsquo;s completion system. When you type&#10;&lt;code&gt;treemand [Tab]&lt;/code&gt;, it suggests CLI names from the discovery cache — so the more&#10;CLIs you explore, the more useful tab-completion becomes.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>mcp</title><link>/commands/mcp/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/commands/mcp/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="treemand-mcp"&gt;&lt;code&gt;treemand mcp&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Run a &lt;a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io"&gt;Model Context Protocol&lt;/a&gt; server on stdin&#10;and stdout. An AI agent connected to it can map any command-line tool on your&#10;&lt;code&gt;PATH&lt;/code&gt; without running &lt;code&gt;--help&lt;/code&gt; and parsing the text itself.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="connect-a-client"&gt;Connect a client &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#connect-a-client" aria-label="Link to this section: Connect a client"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The server is a local stdio process, started by the client:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;claude mcp add treemand -- treemand mcp&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Clients configured with JSON take the same command:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>doctor</title><link>/commands/doctor/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/commands/doctor/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="treemand-doctor"&gt;&lt;code&gt;treemand doctor&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;When a tree looks wrong or a run is slow, &lt;code&gt;treemand doctor &amp;lt;cli&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; shows what&#10;happened. It discovers the CLI afresh (the cache is neither read nor written)&#10;and reports:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;the treemand version, platform, binary, strategy and the help form the CLI&#10;answered (&lt;code&gt;--help&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;-h&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;how many commands were found, and which have no description, no flags, or&#10;were left undiscovered (stubs)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;commands whose help could not be read, and why&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;the &lt;a href="../config/#overrides-for-clis-treemand-misreads"&gt;override file&lt;/a&gt;, if you&#10;have one for the CLI, and how many changes it made (the counts above include&#10;them)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;every help probe by outcome (ok, non-zero exit, timed out, cancelled, failed,&#10;truncated) and the five slowest&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="usage"&gt;Usage &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#usage" aria-label="Link to this section: Usage"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand doctor git&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;treemand doctor: git&#10;&#10; treemand v0.14.0 (darwin/arm64)&#10; binary /opt/homebrew/bin/git&#10; strategy help&#10; help form --help&#10; depth 3&#10; elapsed 1.928s&#10;&#10;Tree&#10; nodes 25&#10; without description 0&#10; without flags 0&#10; undiscovered stubs 0&#10; discovery errors 0&#10;&#10;Probes&#10; run 25 (ok 25, non-zero exit 0, timed out 0, cancelled 0, failed 0, truncated 0)&#10; slowest probes&#10; 1.476s ok git reset --help&#10; 1.303s ok git status --help&#10; 463ms ok git branch --help&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;The text report is plain and meant to be pasted into a&#10;&lt;a href="https://github.com/aallbrig/treemand/issues"&gt;bug report&lt;/a&gt;. A binary under your&#10;home directory is shown as &lt;code&gt;~/...&lt;/code&gt;. Lists longer than ten commands are cut short;&#10;&lt;code&gt;--output=json&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;yaml&lt;/code&gt;) prints the full report for scripts:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>history</title><link>/commands/history/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/commands/history/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="treemand-history"&gt;&lt;code&gt;treemand history&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;treemand remembers the commands you copy or run from the&#10;&lt;a href="../interactive/"&gt;interactive TUI&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+E&lt;/code&gt;), one list per CLI. Use them two&#10;ways:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;In the TUI, press &lt;code&gt;Ctrl+R&lt;/code&gt; to see the recent commands for the CLI you are&#10;exploring. &lt;code&gt;Enter&lt;/code&gt; loads one into the preview bar, ready to edit, copy or&#10;run again.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;From the shell, &lt;code&gt;treemand history &amp;lt;cli&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; prints them, most recent first, one&#10;per line:&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand &lt;span class="nb"&gt;history&lt;/span&gt; git&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand &lt;span class="nb"&gt;history&lt;/span&gt; kubectl --output json &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# with use counts and timestamps&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="where-it-lives"&gt;Where it lives &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#where-it-lives" aria-label="Link to this section: Where it lives"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;History stays on your machine. Each CLI has a small JSON file under&#10;&lt;code&gt;~/.treemand/history/&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;$TREEMAND_CACHE_DIR/history/&lt;/code&gt;), capped at the 100&#10;most recently used commands. A command used again moves to the top and its&#10;count goes up. Nothing is sent anywhere.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Getting Started</title><link>/getting-started/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/getting-started/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="getting-started"&gt;Getting Started&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="explore-any-cli"&gt;Explore Any CLI &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#explore-any-cli" aria-label="Link to this section: Explore Any CLI"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Point treemand at a CLI tool and it maps out the full command hierarchy:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand git &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# explore git&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand kubectl &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# explore kubectl&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand aws &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# explore the AWS CLI&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;treemand treemand &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# introspect treemand itself&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="output-formats"&gt;Output Formats &lt;a class="anchor" data-pagefind-ignore href="#output-formats" aria-label="Link to this section: Output Formats"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;treemand produces three output formats — a human-readable tree for your&#10;terminal, plus JSON and YAML for piping into scripts and tools:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Installation</title><link>/installation/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/installation/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="installation"&gt;Installation&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Pick your system and copy the commands. We guess your system from your browser; use the buttons to change it. The install script verifies each release&amp;rsquo;s signature and checksum, and nothing here needs admin rights unless you ask for &lt;code&gt;--system&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="install-picker" id="install-picker"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="os-switch" id="os-switch" role="group" aria-label="Show install steps for" hidden&gt;&#10; &lt;button type="button" class="os-btn" data-os="macos" aria-pressed="false"&gt;macOS&lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;button type="button" class="os-btn" data-os="linux" aria-pressed="false"&gt;Linux&lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;button type="button" class="os-btn" data-os="windows" aria-pressed="false"&gt;Windows&lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="os-detected" id="os-detected" role="status" hidden&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;section class="os-panel" id="install-macos" data-os="macos" aria-labelledby="install-macos-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;h2 id="install-macos-title"&gt;macOS&lt;/h2&gt;&#10; &lt;article class="channel recommended"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Homebrew &lt;span class="tag"&gt;Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Installs and updates treemand and its man page.&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="cmd"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;brew tap aallbrig/tap&#10;brew install treemand&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/article&gt;&#10; &lt;article class="channel"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Install script&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Downloads the release for your Mac (Apple Silicon or Intel), verifies its signature (with cosign) and SHA-256 checksum, and installs to &lt;code&gt;~/.local/bin&lt;/code&gt;. No admin rights needed.&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="cmd"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl -fsSL https://treemand.dev/install.sh | sh&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/article&gt;&#10; &lt;article class="channel"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Release binary&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Download &lt;code&gt;treemand_darwin_arm64.tar.gz&lt;/code&gt; (Apple Silicon) or &lt;code&gt;treemand_darwin_amd64.tar.gz&lt;/code&gt; (Intel) from the &lt;a href="https://github.com/aallbrig/treemand/releases/latest"&gt;latest release&lt;/a&gt;, then:&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="cmd"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;tar xzf treemand_darwin_arm64.tar.gz&#10;mv treemand_darwin_arm64 /usr/local/bin/treemand&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/article&gt;&#10; &lt;article class="channel"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Go (from source)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Needs Go 1.26 or newer. Builds the current source; the binary lands in &lt;code&gt;$GOPATH/bin&lt;/code&gt; (usually &lt;code&gt;~/go/bin&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="cmd"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/aallbrig/treemand.git &amp;amp;&amp;amp; cd treemand/cli/treemand &amp;amp;&amp;amp; go install .&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/article&gt;&#10; &lt;/section&gt;&#10; &lt;section class="os-panel" id="install-linux" data-os="linux" aria-labelledby="install-linux-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;h2 id="install-linux-title"&gt;Linux&lt;/h2&gt;&#10; &lt;article class="channel recommended"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Install script &lt;span class="tag"&gt;Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Downloads the release for your CPU (amd64 or arm64), verifies its signature (with cosign) and SHA-256 checksum, and installs to &lt;code&gt;~/.local/bin&lt;/code&gt; with the man page. No root needed; add &lt;code&gt;--system&lt;/code&gt; for &lt;code&gt;/usr/local/bin&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="cmd"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl -fsSL https://treemand.dev/install.sh | sh&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/article&gt;&#10; &lt;article class="channel"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Homebrew&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Works with Homebrew on Linux.&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="cmd"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;brew tap aallbrig/tap&#10;brew install treemand&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/article&gt;&#10; &lt;article class="channel"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Release binary&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Download &lt;code&gt;treemand_linux_amd64.tar.gz&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;treemand_linux_arm64.tar.gz&lt;/code&gt; from the &lt;a href="https://github.com/aallbrig/treemand/releases/latest"&gt;latest release&lt;/a&gt;, check it against &lt;code&gt;checksums.txt&lt;/code&gt;, then:&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="cmd"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;sha256sum -c --ignore-missing checksums.txt&#10;tar xzf treemand_linux_amd64.tar.gz&#10;install -m 0755 treemand_linux_amd64 ~/.local/bin/treemand&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/article&gt;&#10; &lt;article class="channel"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Go (from source)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Needs Go 1.26 or newer. Builds the current source; the binary lands in &lt;code&gt;$GOPATH/bin&lt;/code&gt; (usually &lt;code&gt;~/go/bin&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="cmd"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/aallbrig/treemand.git &amp;amp;&amp;amp; cd treemand/cli/treemand &amp;amp;&amp;amp; go install .&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/article&gt;&#10; &lt;/section&gt;&#10; &lt;section class="os-panel" id="install-windows" data-os="windows" aria-labelledby="install-windows-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;h2 id="install-windows-title"&gt;Windows&lt;/h2&gt;&#10; &lt;article class="channel recommended"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Release binary (PowerShell) &lt;span class="tag"&gt;Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Downloads the zip, unpacks it into &lt;code&gt;%USERPROFILE%\bin&lt;/code&gt; and names it &lt;code&gt;treemand.exe&lt;/code&gt;. Add that folder to your &lt;code&gt;PATH&lt;/code&gt;. These steps are not run in CI. In WSL, use the Linux install script instead.&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="cmd"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;$dir = &amp;#34;$env:USERPROFILE\bin&amp;#34;; New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force $dir | Out-Null&#10;$v = (Invoke-RestMethod https://treemand.dev/releases/latest.txt).Trim()&#10;Invoke-WebRequest &amp;#34;https://treemand.dev/releases/$v/treemand_windows_amd64.zip&amp;#34; -OutFile treemand.zip&#10;Expand-Archive -Force treemand.zip -DestinationPath $dir&#10;Move-Item -Force &amp;#34;$dir\treemand_windows_amd64.exe&amp;#34; &amp;#34;$dir\treemand.exe&amp;#34;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/article&gt;&#10; &lt;article class="channel"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Go (from source)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Needs Go 1.26 or newer. Builds the current source; the binary lands in &lt;code&gt;%GOPATH%\bin&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="cmd"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/aallbrig/treemand.git; cd treemand\cli\treemand; go install .&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/article&gt;&#10; &lt;/section&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Try It</title><link>/try/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/try/</guid><description/></item></channel></rss>